after more research with AI "which filename used by APT28 collects credentials?""

artifact seen during specific intrusions where APT28 used credential harvesting + local staging (often under C:\ProgramData\ or similar writable system paths).

so we know that the file has to be stored in  C:\ProgramData\

1. Look for files created shortly after the archives

let Downloads =
FileCreationEvents
| where filename in ("photo.zip","IOC_30_08.rar","details.zip")
| project hostname, DownloadTime=timestamp;
FileCreationEvents
| join kind=inner Downloads on hostname
| where timestamp between (DownloadTime .. DownloadTime + 30m)
| project timestamp, hostname, filename, path
| order by hostname, timestamp

///C:\ProgramData\

2. search file under  C:\ProgramData\

FileCreationEvents
| where path contains @"C:\ProgramData\"
| distinct path

